**Description:**

When working with threads i'm trying to get the context around an in-thread event. For that purpose i'm passing the `filter` parameter as:
```
{"io.element.relation_types":["io.element.thread"]}
```
, like we'll do for `/messages` api as recommended in [MSC3440](https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-doc/blob/gsouquet/threading-via-relations/proposals/3440-threading-via-relations.md#fetch-all-threads-in-a-room)

But the api does not seem to honor that and returns a response like below in `events_after` or `events_before`. So not only returning in-thread events but also other events too. I was expecting to get only in-thread events.
